{
  "summary": "This multimodal multiprofile experiment (scvi_n200, ResNet50, transformer aggregation, concat fusion) achieved a validation accuracy of 0.688 (F1: 0.659), a ~5.6-point improvement over the otherwise identical avgpool configuration (0.632, F1: 0.607; llm_summary_006), indicating that a learned, position-aware transformer aggregation captures inter-profile interaction signal that symmetric averaging discards. Because the only change was the aggregation method, the result isolates aggregation design as a consequential axis beyond the multiprofile data-volume gain and establishes transformer as the preferred default for subsequent experiments. It remains uncertain whether further aggregation architectures could yield additional gains, whether the observed improvement is stable across random initializations, and how this choice interacts with alternative encoders or fusion strategies."
}

